  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $6.9B on federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice awarded 40,233 contracts, with an average award size of $171K. Obligations fell 19.5% year over year. Yearly comparisons show FY21 $9.1B, FY22 $9B, FY23 $10B, FY24 $9.4B, FY25 $8.5B, and FY26 $6.9B. Other Computer Related Services is the largest NAICS category to date at $818M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $755M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $612M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor to date at $515M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $176M and AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $149M. The top ten categories and the top ten vendors together account for a substantial share of FY2026 contract obligations. Contract types include recurring services such as medical care, security, IT services, and facilities support. Fiscal year totals are partial and represent obligations through the current fiscal year to date, so FY2026 figures remain incomplete for the full year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Justice spending trended year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $6.9B in FY26 to date, down 19.5% year over year. Annual obligations were FY21 $9.1B, FY22 $9B, FY23 $10B, FY24 $9.4B, FY25 $8.5B, and FY26 $6.9B. The average award size in FY26 to date is $171K across 40,233 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Justice's biggest buys and vendors this year?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services leads NAICS categories at $818M, with Security Guards and Patrol Services at $755M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $612M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. leads vendors at $515M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $176M and AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $149M. Categories also include Other Residential Care Facilities, Computer Systems Design Services, and All Other Legal Services."
      }
    ]
  },
